From 28865eff8981ba35b50739b1d50140137ad3c3f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakshman Turlapati <lakshmanturlapati@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 19:21:13 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] test(22-05): retain built-app extension smoke bootstrap,
 controller, and manager-caller RED contract

- Add PrometheusExtensionSmokeBootstrap: non-official, exact
  --test-type=prometheus-runtime, disposable-profile, no-follow owner-only
  0600 launch-config validation plus fixture directory/manifest SHA-256
  verification, mirroring the existing runtime/supervision test bootstraps.
- Add PrometheusExtensionSmokeController: one-shot native chrome://extensions
  lifecycle drive (manager open, developer-mode toggle, Load unpacked click,
  inspect/reload/disable/enable/remove, local policy grant matrix, options
  routing) that never calls UnpackedInstaller/ExtensionRegistrar directly.
  Installs a one-shot ui::SelectFileDialogFactory immediately before the real
  Load-unpacked click that self-clears in Create() (never answers a second or
  unrelated picker) and only delivers the bootstrap-verified fixture
  directory when Browser/window/caller/type/title/stage all match exactly.
- Compose the bootstrap+controller from PrometheusBrowserMainExtraParts via a
  new BrowserCollectionObserver-based waiter, gated only on the exact
  extension-smoke command-line switch, independent of the Agent gateway path.
- Add prometheus_extension_smoke_browsertest.cc: full-lifecycle and
  Create()-denial (OTR profile, mismatched browser/profile, early shutdown)
  browser tests, plus a real-tab developer-private caller pair.
- Retain the developer-private committed-caller RED/GREEN contract as
  TEST_F cases in developer_private_api_unittest.cc (source-retained; see
  verify-phase-22-extension-smoke.sh for why this binary instead executes
  the browser-test copy).
- RED: the full-lifecycle controller test correctly halts at
  kLoadUnpackedClicked (install_not_observed_timeout) because
  DeveloperPrivateLoadUnpackedFunction::ShowSelectFileDialog() does not yet
  pass a caller; the one committed-caller browser test asserting a non-null
  caller fails accordingly. A later plan lands the narrow developer-private
  change that flips both green.
